abstract: >-
  Julia/Gurobi implementation of a bilevel (Stackelberg) model in which the state
  sets renovation-subsidy rates by measure, income group and tenure to bring a
  national residential building stock onto its EPBD primary-energy trajectory at
  minimum public spending, while owner-occupiers and public and private landlords
  decide on renovation in their own economic interest. Poland case, census stock,
  fixed 2020-2025 history, design from 2026. The release contains the model code,
  the search and local-proof scripts, the input data (except third-party source
  documents), the pl12 results of record (all run folders, certificate logs,
  summary tables, figures) and the review follow-ups of November 2026.
